---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { getState, href } from '../../lib/data';
import { breadcrumbNode, pageGraph, webPageNode } from '../../lib/schema';

const title = 'Georgia HOA rules for an RV or boat | RV Storage Finder';
const description =
  'No Georgia statute was found that names an RV, a boat, or driveway parking as something a property owners’ association must allow or must forbid. Not legal advice.';
const path = '/rules/georgia/';
const checked = '2026-11-19';
const georgia = getState('georgia');
const crumbs = [
  { label: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { label: 'HOA rules', path: '/rules/' },
  { label: 'Georgia', path },
];
const schema = pageGraph([
  webPageNode({ title, description, path, dateModified: checked }),
  breadcrumbNode(crumbs),
]);
---

<Base title={title} description={description} path={path} schema={schema}>
  <article class="wrap prose">
    <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
    <h1>Georgia HOA rules for an RV or boat</h1>
    <p>
      This page is not legal advice. On <time datetime={checked}>November 19, 2026</time>, no Georgia
      statute was found that names a recreational vehicle, motor home, boat, or driveway parking rule
      as something a property owners’ association must allow or must forbid.
    </p>
    <p>
      The association statute is the Georgia Property Owners’ Association Act, Article 6 of Chapter 3
      of Title 44 of the Official Code of Georgia Annotated. The
      <a href="https://www.legis.ga.gov/laws" rel="noopener noreferrer">Georgia General Assembly laws page</a>
      did not return the code text during this review, so this page does not quote a section of that
      article. Secondary reprints of the article were not used as the statute.
    </p>
    <h2>What that finding does not decide</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        No statute found is not a statement that an association may not adopt a parking rule. The
        recorded instrument, the bylaws, and any rules the instrument allows still have to be read.
      </li>
      <li>
        This page does not decide whether a particular association is governed by Article 6. That
        question is in the recorded instrument and in the Act’s applicability section, which this
        review did not quote.
      </li>
      <li>
        A city or county ordinance can still regulate parking. This page does not read one.
      </li>
      <li>
        A community rule, a covenant PDF, or a law-firm summary is not a statute. None of those was
        treated as the Code.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Off-site storage is a different question</h2>
    <p>
      A facility listing in this directory is a storage lot, not a statement that an association allows
      the vehicle at the house. {georgia.cities.length} Georgia city pages list those lots.
    </p>
    <ul>
      {
        georgia.cities.map((city) => (
          <li>
            <a href={href(`/cities/${city.id}/`)}>
              {city.city}, {city.state_code}
            </a>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </article>
</Base>
